// array_size_intcast_range.z98 — standalone reproduction for the Task 11S (a) fix.
//
// Compile (seed-built zig1 with its sibling lib/):
//   <zig1> -ffast --dump-c89 --output-dir /tmp/arrcast repro/array_size_intcast_range.z98
//   echo "dump rc=$?"   # expect 2
//
// DEFECT (Task 11F regression): `evalConstU32Full`'s `@intCast` arm in an
// array-size position folded the operand (extra-child 1) and IGNORED the target
// type (extra-child 0), so `var a: [@intCast(u8, 300)]u8` folded to length 300
// and compiled cleanly (rc=0, 0 diagnostics) — a silent miscompile. Official
// Zig and the Z98 spec reject `@intCast(u8, 300)`: 300 does not fit u8.
//
// FIX (Task 11S): the arm resolves the target type, folds the operand via the
// U32 evaluator (so a function-local `const N` still resolves), and requires
// `intValueFitsType(env, target, v)`; otherwise it emits error[3000] and
// returns the unfoldable sentinel.
//
// EXPECTED after the fix: dump rc=2, 0 `.c`, and a primary
//   error[3000]: @intCast value does not fit the target type
// (the array-size arm additionally reports its pre-existing error[3050]
// cascade for the same source). Positive controls live in
// `repro/mi_matrix/stdlib_intcast_range_xmod`.
var a: [@intCast(u8, 300)]u8 = undefined;

pub fn main() void {
    _ = a;
}
